<title>FINLAND: Borealis,  Nova Chemicals plan JV.</title>
<headline>Borealis,  Nova Chemicals plan JV.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borealis, a petrochemicals venture jointly owned by Finland's Neste Oy and Norway's Statoil, said on Thursday it had agreed with Canada's  Nova Chemicals to form a joint venture for American markets.</p>
<p>&quot;The company's purpose is to produce and market polyethylene plastics for cable applications for the North and South American markets,&quot; Borealis said in a statement.</p>
<p>It and Nova will each own a 50 percent stake in the planned venture, due to begin operations in January 1997, Borealis said; it did not specify where it would be headquartered.</p>
<p>The deal has yet to be approved by the boards of directors of both companies and possibly some authorities, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 80 6805 0247</p>
</text>
